A||N||11||87ECO5||Is it just me, or does Mother Nature hate me for having a Fiero!?||||8||
Z||000000||87ECO5||09-10-2000||08:52 PM||||Well, this is two weeks in a row now that I've missed an opportunity to show my car because of rain!<P>Last weekend, I set out to wash my car for the monthly car show in Springboro.  As soon as I dried it off, it began to rain.  Somewhat flustered, I waited until it stopped then dried the car again.  Got the last few drops wiped off and it began to rain again!  Now, I'm ticked!  After throwing a few inanimate objects, I waited until it stopped and dried it off again.  This time, it didn't wait until I was finished.  Instead, it dumped on me right in the middle of everything!  After throwing a few more things and saying a few choice words to our holy weather goddess, I "stormed" inside to inform my wife we wouldn't be going to the show.<P>One hour later, we were across the street from the car show grabbing a bite to eat when the clouds broke and the sun appeared!<P>Today was COFE's September outing, which I had planned to attend.  So, I headed to the local car wash yesterday evening to vacuum out the Fiero.  Keep in mind, the day had been beautiful up to now.  I pulled in, opened the car, dropped quarters into the vacuum machine and ... HOLY COW!!!!!  Out of nowhere, a major downpour - or should I say sidepour!?  Heavy rain, coming into the car - FROM THE SIDE!  The interior got completely soaked!  I buttoned her up, drove her home, pulled into the driveway and ... SON OF A B!T@#!!!!!  The sun appeared!<P>After a few more choice words to her holiness, I took a trip to the back yard to inform my wife that I'd prepare the Fiero in the morning!<P>Here's where I go off on The Weather Channel!  I wake up this morning, turn on TWC and proceed to cry as they say to expect showers (heavy at times) most of the day.  After telling my wife we weren't going to the COFE outing, and deciding to make other plans, the sun appeared and it never did rain!<P>Somebody doesn't want me to show my car!  BTW, does anyone have Mother Nature's email address!?  I'd like to send her a nice note ... ya, that's it ... a nice note ... yaaaa ... that's the ticket!<P>Sorry for the long note.  Thanks for letting me vent!||||reg||8
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-10-2000||08:56 PM||||I know it sucks, but be thankful for rain! We're over 26 inches defecit for the year on rain..some places like Texas are even worse.<BR>I would welcome rain right now, if I could remember what it was!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-10-2000||08:59 PM||||Mother Nature must drive an MR2.  I've been trying for 2 weeks to replace my brake lines.  Either I stay late at work (on the sunny days, of course) or it rains.  I had the entire day off today (down to 6 days a week <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) and what did it do?  Yup.  Rained the entire day...until it got dark.  Then it quit and the clouds went away.  I may just take my car down to the local shop and pay to have them do it.  I'm starting to leak some brake fluid.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||09-10-2000||09:27 PM||||Vent away.  I moved last year from just a few miles from 'Boro.  Went thru there every day.  Lived around there 14 years & would be there now except needed the kids to be closer to relatives.  Moving back when I retire (as if).  Very pretty area there, but gotta sympathize with your frustration.||||reg||4
Z||000004||ChadMan||09-11-2000||09:58 AM||||We missed you at the COFE meeting, but don't beat yourself up - it rained cats and dogs here yesterday.  About 10 people showed up but only two of us drove our Fieros.  We didn't go putt-putting because of the rain.<P>So you would have driven 4 hours round-trip for 90 minutes of good Fiero-related conversation and subpar fast food.  We're all nice people here at COFE but not THAT nice!||||reg||9
